codex
Implemented and verified a native `TRACK = "B"` problem generator based on Lemma 2.1 of [arXiv:1906.09291](https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.09291).

Key results:

- All G1–G9 gates pass.
- Exact guess probability: `4 / 7,206,672 ≈ 5.55e-7`.
- Five adversarial attacks: `0/8` successes each.
- Reference traversal: 18,376,459 operations, median 1.90 seconds.
- Compact structural route: 265 operations.
- Oracle results: bare `0/3`, hinted `0/3`, placebo `0/3`.
- Answer size: at most 35 characters, 9 estimated tokens, 5 elements.

Deliverables:

- [gen_1906_09291.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.09291/gen_1906_09291.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.09291/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.09291/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.09291/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.09291/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.09291/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The final import, interface, profile, transcript-schema, JSON round-trip, and canonical-key audits all passed.
